    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0710" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1102</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tiflis</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tiflis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-15T18:00:00+02:59"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 16, 1.56
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Enver Pasha<anchor n="1" xml:id="d737-f1"/> telegraphs to commander in chief here
                    informing him that in view of the Armenian raids and atrocities against
                    Mohammedans he is constrained to resume offensive. Few Armenian troops holding
                    front, scarcely will be able to resist an advance but have been advised to fall
                    back in order, destroying supplies, which I believe form main object of Turkish
                    threat.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d737-f1" n="1" xml:id="d737-f1-content">
                <p>Turkish Minister of War.</p>
